This is a generated, numeric-answer adaptation. The basic curriculum uses
algebra__linear_1d and polynomials__evaluate. The composed curriculum uses
algebra__linear_1d_composed, polynomials__evaluate_composed, algebra__linear_2d
and algebra__linear_2d_composed. The selected modules and curriculum appear in
source_manifest.json. This is not the complete published Mathematics Dataset, an
official test set, or a reproduction of published benchmark scores. The recipe
uses exact rational equivalence, rather than the paper's answer-string metric.

For composed generation only, expand_entities is adapted from the pinned
DeepMind source to sort descriptions before its seeded shuffle. This removes
object-address-dependent statement ordering without changing mathematical
generators or gold answers. The adapter version is recorded in the manifest.
